{"id":"c4d2f7264607dcc1","group":"68","path":"68/68-thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem.md","title":"Shoenfield Recursion Theorem","display":"thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem — Shoenfield Recursion Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem","aliases":["68-thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem"],"display":"thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem — Shoenfield Recursion Theorem","depends_on":["[[68-df-number-theoretic-function]]","[[68-df-kleene-normal-form]]","[[68-df-partial-recursive-function-class]]","[[68-thm-s-m-n-theorem]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"§8.7 p.25 / PDF 34","verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"source-proof-reviewed","revision_basis":"supplied-68(1).zip; local content, type, and dependency review"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-shoenfield-recursion-theorem — Shoenfield Recursion Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c524671590651be2\" href=\"?note=c524671590651be2\" title=\"68-df-number-theoretic-function\">68-df-number-theoretic-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bca7d0eca4017dc7\" href=\"?note=bca7d0eca4017dc7\" title=\"68-df-kleene-normal-form\">68-df-kleene-normal-form</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5f5b8b347f696f58\" href=\"?note=5f5b8b347f696f58\" title=\"68-df-partial-recursive-function-class\">68-df-partial-recursive-function-class</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"3b8f02ef6e351ea3\" href=\"?note=3b8f02ef6e351ea3\" title=\"68-thm-s-m-n-theorem\">68-thm-s-m-n-theorem</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"§8.7 p.25 / PDF 34"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source-proof-reviewed"},{"key":"revision_basis","html":"supplied-68(1).zip; local content, type, and dependency review"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(k\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_{k+1}\">\\(G\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_{k+1}\\)</span>，输入为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vec x\\,^{\\frown}\\langle e\\rangle\">\\(\\vec x\\,^{\\frown}\\langle e\\rangle\\)</span>，连接算子见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c524671590651be2\" href=\"?note=c524671590651be2\" title=\"68-df-number-theoretic-function\">68-df-number-theoretic-function</a>。函数类与索引见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5f5b8b347f696f58\" href=\"?note=5f5b8b347f696f58\" title=\"68-df-partial-recursive-function-class\">68-df-partial-recursive-function-class</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"bca7d0eca4017dc7\" href=\"?note=bca7d0eca4017dc7\" title=\"68-df-kleene-normal-form\">68-df-kleene-normal-form</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\simeq\">\\(\\simeq\\)</span> 是偏值相等。</p>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal F_k\">\\(\\mathcal F_k\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"c524671590651be2\" href=\"?note=c524671590651be2\" title=\"68-df-number-theoretic-function\">68-df-number-theoretic-function</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\exists f\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^k\\;(\\varphi_f^{(k)}(\\vec x)\\simeq G(\\vec x\\,^{\\frown}\\langle f\\rangle)).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\exists f\\in\\mathbb N\\;\\forall\\vec x\\in\\mathbb N^k\\;(\\varphi_f^{(k)}(\\vec x)\\simeq G(\\vec x\\,^{\\frown}\\langle f\\rangle)).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>直接对应 8.7 Recursion Theorem，印刷 p.25 / PDF p.34，而非只记录一个索引变换器推论。由参数定理取全递归 S 使 φ_{S(y)}<sup>(k)(x)≃φ_y</sup>(k+1)(x,y)。令 H(x,y)≃G(x,S(y))，取 H 的索引 h，并置 f=S(h)，代入即得 φ_f(x)≃φ_h(x,h)≃G(x,S(h))=G(x,f)。所有等号均按偏值相等理解，故 G 无须全定义。原书证明已逐步复核。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-number-theoretic-function","status":"resolved","id":"c524671590651be2","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-number-theoretic-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-kleene-normal-form","status":"resolved","id":"bca7d0eca4017dc7","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-kleene-normal-form]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-partial-recursive-function-class","status":"resolved","id":"5f5b8b347f696f58","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-partial-recursive-function-class]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-thm-s-m-n-theorem","status":"resolved","id":"3b8f02ef6e351ea3","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-thm-s-m-n-theorem]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-number-theoretic-function","status":"resolved","id":"c524671590651be2","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$k\\in\\mathbb N$，$G\\in\\mathrm{PartRec}\\cap\\mathcal F_{k+1}$，输入为 $\\vec x\\,^{\\frown}\\langle e\\ran